@inject ApiMetadata Api
@* Card's Overview, written by hand after Button's and Form's: the header and variants, sizes, a
   linked card with media, a heading of your own, the body and footer, flush content, sections, a
   form in a card (each mode posts it differently) and a grid of cards. Accessibility, Parts and
   See also come from the doc comment and components.json. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A card frames one thing people look at or act on, such as a project, a person or a plan, and often sits in a grid with others like it. For a band across the page, such as a hero, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/section">Section</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Variants</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Variant</Code> for <Code>Outline</Code> (the default), <Code>Elevated</Code> or <Code>Filled</Code>, and <Code>Title</Code> and <Code>Description</Code> for the header.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="card-variants" />
<TextBlock>The title is an <Code>h3</Code>; set <Code>TitleLevel</Code> to fit the page's outline. Content between the tags is the body.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Sizes</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Size</Code> for the padding and the title's size (<Code>Md</Code> by default): <Code>Sm</Code> for dense grids, <Code>Lg</Code> for a card on its own.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="card-sizes" />

<Heading Level="2">A linked card</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Href</Code> to make the whole card a link through its title; buttons in <Code>CardActions</Code>, <Code>CardFooter</Code> and the body stay clickable on their own.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="card-linked" />
<TextBlock>The link is the title, so a linked card needs a <Code>Title</Code>. <Code>CardMedia</Code> draws an image, video or SVG across the top, edge to edge; one that only decorates gets <Code>alt=""</Code> on an <Code>img</Code> or <Code>aria-hidden="true"</Code> on an <Code>svg</Code>. On a linked card an image is part of the link, and a video's controls stay usable above it.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Your own heading</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>CardHeader</Code> for content above the title, such as who wrote it, and <Code>CardActions</Code> for buttons or a <Anchor Href="docs/components/menu">Menu</Anchor> at the end of the heading row.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="card-post" />

<Heading Level="2">Body and footer</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>CardBody</Code> for the body's layout, with <Code>Gap</Code>, <Code>Align</Code> and <Code>Direction</Code>, and <Code>CardFooter</Code> for a row of buttons at the bottom, with <Code>Justify</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="card-footer" />
<TextBlock>Write the footer last, directly in the card: inside a <Code>CardBody</Code> or a form it's an ordinary row, not the card's footer.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Flush content</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Flush</Code> on a <Code>CardBody</Code> to run a <Anchor Href="docs/components/table">Table</Anchor> or a divided list to the card's edges.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="card-flush" />

<Heading Level="2">Sections and a footer bar</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Dividers</Code> to make each <Code>CardBody</Code> a section with a line between, and give the <Code>CardFooter</Code> a <Code>Bg</Code> or <Code>BorderTop</Code> to make it a bar across the bottom.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="card-sections" />

<Heading Level="2">A form in a card</Heading>
<TextBlock>Put the <Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor> around the card, so the submit button in its <Code>CardFooter</Code> is inside the form.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="card-settings" />
<TextBlock>A <Code>CardFooter</Code> inside a form isn't drawn as the card's footer, and <Code>CardMedia</Code>, <Code>CardHeader</Code> and <Code>CardActions</Code> are drawn at the card's level, so a form inside the card reaches none of them. A form whose buttons are in its own <Code>FormActions</Code> can go inside.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Cards in a grid</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/grid">Grid</Anchor> with <Code>MinChildWidth</Code> to fit as many cards to a row as there's room for. Cards in a row take its height, and a <Code>CardFooter</Code> stays at the bottom.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="card-projects" />
<TextBlock>Put the body's text in an element, such as a <Code>TextBlock</Code>: above a footer, bare text gets the body's gap, not a section's space.</TextBlock>

@if (OverviewParts.Of(Component, Api).Count > 0)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Parts</Heading>
}
<OverviewParts Component="Component" />

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <Card Title="Website" Description="Updated 2 hours ago">
            <TextBlock>Marketing pages and the docs, deployed from main.</TextBlock>
            <CardFooter Justify="Justify.End">
                <Button Href="projects/website" Size="ControlSize.Sm">Open</Button>
            </CardFooter>
        </Card>

        @* The whole card is a link, through its title. *@
        <Card Title="Course app" Description="12 lessons" Href="courses/app" />
        """;
}
